Commit:     ember arlynx <tobb@ember.software>
CommitDate: Sun Oct 18 04:39:57 2026 -0400

    kernel!: rows — keyed, bounded rows under an object, the fourth trie; heads count and sum their rows and are never pinned, so two inserts into one relation commute; a range read is pinned by its listing and supplies exactly the rows under its prefix in key order (KERNEL-46/48, LANG-44/49, CODEC-33/34, HOST-44, PROTOCOL-45 receipt re-cut)
    
    One day, four halves: kernel (KERNEL-15/16/17), codec (CODEC-9/10), lang (LANG-14), host (HOST-12); protocol receipt re-cut (PROTOCOL-10).
    
    What shape changed:
    - World gains `rows`, a fourth instance of the one trie (rowSpec: routed by rowKeyBytes, depth rowDepth = 280 + 8·keyBytesMax). Keys: head = parent‖rel‖0; row = parent‖rel‖1‖|k|‖k (length-prefixed, so the encoding is prefix-free). Leaves: head (count sum limit cap width retract) | row (amt val).
    - Turn gains `rows : List RowTouch` and `ranges : List RangeRead` (last two fields). RowAct = declare | insert | upsert | retract | keep. Two pin kinds: a row pin (the leaf digest or the absence digest) and a range pin (rangePin: the listing's count, then each row's key bytes and leaf digest, in key order).
    - Admission (check): … checkNullifiers, checkRowsRemain, checkRanges, rowsRun, checkCharge(credit + rows freed), checkCreates, checkSteps. Rows are charged (Turn.growth counts row touches; World.weight = cellsWeight + rowsWeight; upsert/retract credit back; fold_conserves exact) and carried (Carried.rows, last field; the carry origin commits the rows root; checkCarry bounds cells+rows+allowance).
    - rootsDigest takes FOUR roots (cells, journal, refusals, rows) in the head link; the receipt (PROTOCOL-45) carries `rowsroot`.
    - Strengthenings found while proving (ROOT accepted; decisions/kernel.md KERNEL-17 addendum): a row under a parent the same turn retires is refused orphanRow (it was ADMITTED: a row under a tombstone); a retired parent's heads leave with it (dropHeads, weight credited), so every head's parent is live (rowsParented); a range prefix longer than the key width is refused keyWidth (a shorter key routed into the listed subtree made the listing wrong); `under` takes a bound (rangeRows reads most+1; checkRowsRemain reads 257); a declare carrying a pin is refused rowShape (one encoding per effect).
    - Compiled admission: World.admitImpl runs check's rows once and hands them to commit (checkWith/commitWith); `@[csimp] World.admit_eq_admitImpl` proves it equal to the spec World.admit, whose statements are unchanged. insN/insA (a relation's insert count/amount in a touch list) are public defs.
    - Receive (LANG-14, agreed): Unsigned.rowPins/ranges, RowView, Draft.rows, sealTurn → Turn.rows/ranges; create emits declares from Program.rels; receive refusals rowUnpinned rangeUnpinned rangeTooLong rowParent duplicateRow.
    
    What refuses (by name): keyTaken relationFull relationCapped rowParentUnpinned orphanRow rowsRemain keyWidth noRelation retractForbidden declareLate rangeTooLong duplicateRow rowShape, and `stale parent` for a moved row pin or range pin; receive: rowUnpinned rangeUnpinned rangeTooLong rowParent duplicateRow. rejectNames/refusalNames gain them in constructor order, so EVERY recorded reject code shifts (by 5 for the receive refusals first).
    
    What re-geneses / re-emits / refuses to load:
    - Every Store re-geneses. The World wire, the carried wire, the turn, the signed call, the step and the refusal records move their stamps: an old base, an old batch record AND an old carried export refuse by stamp (kernel/world, kernel/carried, kernel/turn, kernel/unsigned, kernel/call …).
    - Re-emitted: gates/codec-vectors.tsv (140 vectors over 48 sites, incl. the kernel-functions section with the 128/129 key boundary; `--check` ok); every package with `rels` re-ids (a seventh node; every method type gains rows + edits); world/{grain/Lifecycle,hosting/Allowance,escrow/Escrow} package texts re-emitted; generated Rust unchanged (emit-rust/-units/-hosting/-broker --check rc 0).
    
    Theorems (each with its tooth; Kernel unless marked):
    - Charging/carry (Kernel/Proofs/Rows.lean, Weight, Budget): rowsRun_weight (rows move by exactly growth less freed, incl. dropHeads_weight), admit/refuse/fold/genesis/carry_rowsCanon, admit_row_pins + rows_stale_refused, admit_range_pins + range_stale_refused.
    - head_sum (Kernel/Proofs/RowsHead.lean): on a World with RowsCanon and RowsOk, a head's count is the number of its rows, its sum their amts' sum, sum ≤ cap, count ≤ limit, every key at the head's width; World.RowsOk = rowFits per entry ∧ rowsHeaded ∧ rowsParented, preserved by genesis/admit/refuse/fold/carry (admit_rowsOk needs E.Lawful: dropHeads and checkRowsRemain list a parent by its id's bytes); deployed_fold_rowsOk discharges both on every reached World; admit_rows_listing (HOST's export bound). Teeth: rowsHeaded_head_bumped, plantInsert_breaks_rowsOk (an insert that bumps the head without the row), rowsParented_orphan_head.
    - range_rows_exact (Kernel/Proofs/RowsRange.lean): the listing a range read is supplied is EXACTLY the rows under rowsPrefix‖pre ((s,v) ∈ l ↔ rowAt = some v ∧ startsWith), strictly ascending by key bytes, and none iff more than `most`; admit_range_exact; fold_range_exact (RowsRangeDeployed: no open premise); under_eq / takeList_eq (the bounded read is the listing cut at n). Teeth: under_needs_long (why keyWidth), rangePinBytes_erase_ne + range_rows_erase_not_exact + range_seal_tooth (a dropped row changes the pin, falsifies exactness, and moves the seal's arg-max), range_rows_satisfiable, range_admit_satisfiable (a concrete admitted turn with a range read, by decide; its dropped-row pin is refused stale).
    - admit_comm (Kernel/Proofs/RowsComm.lean): for t₁ t₂ each admissible from w, footprints disjoint outside heads (RowsCommFoot: insert-only rows on distinct slots, shared cells only `.keep`, no retire, no ranges, distinct tx ids/creates/nullifiers), heads fitting together (RowsFitTogether), both windows at h+2, combined charge ≤ allowance: BOTH orders ADMIT, with equal cells and rows (admit_comm_trie, admit_comm_rows: structural) and additive heads; rowsRun_comm. Teeth: two_rains (premises satisfiable on LANG's two rains), plant_second_rain_stale (a head-pinning insert refuses the second rain), write_repin_refused (a mutation re-pinning the shared cell makes the second refuse stale). Named limit: a range over a relation the other turn inserts into is genuinely order-dependent.
